WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.520
Loaned to us from NHL and New York Rangers, directly from Madison Square Garden ...

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.940
Welcome, forward Mats Zuccarello and goalkeeper Henrik Lundqvist!

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:34.180
It's like ... When we told our crew here who we had booked for the show ...

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.420
They were so impressed!

00:00:37.565 --> 00:00:40.885
The Americans working here were so impressed.

00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:43.825
Last year we had Bruce Springsteen, and that was nothing ...

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.680
... compared to you being here now.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.560
You've got ...

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.800
... a life where you train a lot.

00:00:53.805 --> 00:00:56.815
As far as I know, you've arrived straight from training today.

00:00:56.815 --> 00:00:59.115
Which one of you spends the most time training?

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.040
I think it's me.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.000
No!

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.600
No!

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.640
It's me.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.300
At least on a yearly basis.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.780
It's like this.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.380
A lot of people talk about ...

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.740
... how much you train. But the important thing is really ...

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.740
... how you train. To have a high quality training.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.600
And that ...

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.820
I'm not saying that as a joke.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.260
But the older you get ...

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.400
It's very important to have good quality training so you're not out there too long.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.440
Both on the ice and in the gym, so when you're there you always have a drive.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.720
So I guess I try to have a little more quality than Mats.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.540
So you've got quality training, and you've got quantity training?

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.260
... But not with a very high quality?

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.400
No, the quality isn't very high. I do what's fun!

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.440
And there's not much quality in that. Usually, at least.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.980
How is Zucca perceived ...

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.440
... in the New York Rangers? How does one speak about him, who is he?

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.740
No, but he's ... An incredibly good team mate.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:01.845
Always ...

00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:05.705
Happy, joking around, and he has a good energy ...

00:02:05.705 --> 00:02:07.345
Works hard.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.480
And he's been here so many years that he's also become a leader figure in the team.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.935
It's important that players like that work as hard as him.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.940
So he's sending out good signals.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.320
But he likes to joke around and ...

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.380
To me, he's a little like an annoying little brother, actually.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.540
On the ice.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.620
Why is that?

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.920
The few times he actually scores in training, he's always raising his arms in the air while yelling, and ...

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.560
... and show everyone that he's scored a goal.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.360
It's extremely annoying.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.140
He's rubbing it in?

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.360
Yeah, he rubs it in. Every time!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.960
But does that happen often, that you score?

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.400
Yeah. It's usually quite a lot.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.180
Is it easy to score with him?

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:01.020
No, that's why I cheer, because I'm one of the few people in the world who can score on Henke whenever I want!

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:14.440
How is Henke perceived in the team?

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.840
He's «The King» for everyone else.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.380
Yeah, he is The King.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.980
He definitely is. He is the face of the Rangers and ...

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.320
Like he said ...

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.140
He is our best player.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.760
He's been the Rangers' best player the last 10-12 years.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:41.320
Without him, we wouldn't have the success we've had. Not that we've won, but ...

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.620
We've come a long way.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.720
And like he says, he gets infuriated in trainings whenever someone scores, and ...

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.600
It's that instinct that he has.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.420
Where he hates to lose, and hates to let goals in.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.600
He never quits on a puck.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.080
He's got the winner instinct, and that's ...

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:09.580
Like he said, when he's our biggest guy, it's important the he steps forward and shows that.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.580
Especially when it's not going well. We've had a bad period and ...

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:19.080
... he takes charge and lets us know what he thinks, and people listen to him.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.720
He gets upset?

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.040
He can get a little upset.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.180
He can.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.720
But that goes for all of us.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:30.960
But who is the rest of the team most afraid of?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.560
Of the two of you?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.940
That would be Henrik.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.180
He's a little ...

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.700
... further up the ladder.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.420
When I get mad, I get mad. Yes. And it happens sometimes.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.600
But that can be a mixed blessing.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.420
There's a lot at stake ...

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.640
And ...

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.600
I'm thinking about before a match, when you ...

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.080
When you have to get ready.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.160
There's ... as I've understood, a lot of rituals.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.315
What are those rituals?

00:05:07.315 --> 00:05:10.395
What kind of rituals do you have? What do you need to do every time?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.660
Every time!

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.060
It's actually quite a lot.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:18.200
When I get ready, I have to put on my gloves a certain way. I go through certain things in my head.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:19.480
You have to take on your gloves in a certain way?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.500
Yeah, you know, It's always the catcher first, then the mask.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.000
I bend down, go through certain things in my head.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.500
I'll always do the same, every time. And then ...

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.460
And then it's tome to go out there, and I'll get ready to go out there.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.760
But that procedure ...

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.880
... always happens, within every period.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.840
How about you?

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.800
I guess it's not as bad as him.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.600
I can be pretty annoying and ...

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:48.080
... bother him a lot, but on match day, I talk to him as little as possible.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.740
He's not so social?

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.860
Well, I'm sure he is, but I just ...

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.020
I do not want to be the reason he plays poorly.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.480
So I stay away from him on match days.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.740
So your ritual is really just not to speak to Henke?

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.060
Yes. On match days.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:09.840
And then if we've won and he's played I might bother him for letting in a goal ...

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:16.000
But before matches and during those days I try to keep away ...

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.840
I let him do his own thing, so that I won't say or do anything wrong that makes him play poorly.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:23.800
But I ...

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:26.220
I've got a few rituals.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:30.560
I used to walk to the matches, because I lived quite close to Garden.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:33.275
I would always walk the same route if we won.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.320
And if we lost, I would change the woute, you know. But then ...

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.400
You become a bit crazy in the end.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.740
So you should relax a little with those things.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:43.000
So you would walk certain routes?

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:49.980
Yeah, I would be like «last time, I went that direction, so now I have to go a small detour». But you become ...

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:53.140
... crazy in the end.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.400
So I've calmed down a little.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:01.320
I put on my right skate first. It's not really a ritual, it's ...

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.200
Like Henke says, it's just a force of habit.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.800
It's just how it's become.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:07.940
And then you've got ...

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:11.500
With certain team mates you've got a hand shake here, and ...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.520
... a little dance move with someone there, and then ...

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.920
The last thing ...?

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:16.940
What did you say?

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:18.020
You dance?

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.860
Yeah, we've always got music when we go out, and there's a song at the end and then ...

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:26.400
... there's a dance-off. And if that works, we just keep doing it until ...

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.980
... you lose, and then you change.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:35.040
A couple of years ago, when we had a long winning streak, we had a dance-off ...

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:40.440
Four-five of the guys were dancing to techno music, and ...

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.520
Are you a part of this?

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.420
No, I'm somewhere completely different.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.540
He's not there.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.740
He's not mentally ...

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.420
... in the same world as us.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:53.240
When I'm in my own bubble, they'll be having a dance-off.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.540
Because you want to be by yourself?

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.900
Yes. It's like Mats says, I'm very quiet on match days.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.140
I don't talk a lot.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:06.020
So you'll be moping in the corner, while you're dancing?

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.780
I'm keeping it loose, while he's minding his own.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.780
Can you tell me about ... Now that you're so ...

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.140
... so prominent in the team ...

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.580
It hasn't always been like that, you've both been rookies at one time ...

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.560
What's the difference?

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:31.300
Being a rookie in the New York Rangers, what do you have to put up with, what do you ...

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:37.100
It's changed a little, you notice that some of the young guys coming in, they claim things in a different way.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.015
And our job is really to control this.

00:08:40.015 --> 00:08:43.025
But we don't really do that, we just let it happen.

00:08:43.025 --> 00:08:44.360
Is it a little annoying?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.215
It's just society in general ...

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:51.260
But for example, if it's meal time, and then you go ...

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.080
... to get food, and there's a rookie in front of you.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.920
Then I might say something.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.695
And for instance when we get to the plane, and some of the young people run on the plane first ...

00:08:58.695 --> 00:09:01.515
... and we're at the back waiting with our bags, that's like ...

00:09:02.345 --> 00:09:05.255
Times have changed. Times have changed!

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:06.260
But that's ...

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:11.820
And you've also got those who get it. Who'll stand beside you and wait for their turn.

00:09:14.505 --> 00:09:16.975
But that doesn't happen every time. That's how it is.

00:09:16.975 --> 00:09:19.385
When I first joined the team as young ...

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:24.020
I remember the first time I trained with the Rangers, Henke wasn't there ...

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:27.680
And I got a text message asking if I could shoot at Henke.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:29.140
I was staying at a hotel.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.320
And I was just like «whoah, am I gonna shoot at Henke» ...

00:09:32.505 --> 00:09:35.225
I was scared of him. I was too afraid to speak to him.

00:09:35.225 --> 00:09:37.080
My shots were low.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.020
Close to the ice.

00:09:39.815 --> 00:09:42.265
I was scared of shooting higher.

00:09:42.265 --> 00:09:44.775
But I think that's how it should be.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:47.460
Because you learn to respect others ...

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:48.780
... and your elders.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.720
Mats had a very serious injury.

00:09:53.285 --> 00:09:56.645
You got a fracture in your skull.

00:09:56.765 --> 00:09:58.085
And a bleeding in your brain.

00:09:58.615 --> 00:10:01.565
And I'm just wondering ...

00:10:01.565 --> 00:10:04.705
From your perspective ... I don't know if you were there when it happened?

00:10:04.705 --> 00:10:06.240
Yeah, I played that match.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.420
What do you remember from that incident?

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.260
Well, we didn't quite realize ....

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:14.580
How serious it was, when it happened.

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:19.440
A lot of times, hockey players will get hit by both sticks, pucks and skates ...

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.420
... and ...

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.380
I didn't quite get the full scale of it.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.760
It wasn't before the match was over that we heard how serious it was.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:27.300
Mats can explain himself, but ...

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:30.700
The biggest shock came when I met Mats for the first time after ...

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:31.900
And he had difficulties talking.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.940
Then you really ....

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.740
«Wow. This is ...»

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.100
It could've gone worse ...

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:43.220
But what happened was very serious, so that was a little ...

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.520
... scary.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.940
Did you go to the hospital?

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:52.700
No, we were at home with the kids. But I remember that we facetimed with our daughter.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.880
Tried to joke around a little.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:59.060
I said to him that he usually is quite a handful on the ice anyways ...

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:03.060
So it's quite pleasing that you can't speak right now!

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.020
I remember telling him that.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:09.440
Only as a joke, of course.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:15.120
And looking back, it's wonderful that everything went well, but it was scary the first weeks.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.560
How do you look back on that incident?

00:11:17.715 --> 00:11:21.105
Has it changed you, and has it made you more afraid?

00:11:21.105 --> 00:11:23.985
No. I don't feel that it has.

00:11:23.985 --> 00:11:28.620
The worst part was meeting the guys, and you could see that they just ...

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.540
What the f*ck is he ...

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.620
When I couldn't speak, I couldn't say one word and ...

00:11:34.365 --> 00:11:36.705
So that was hard, but ...

00:11:37.425 --> 00:11:40.165
It ended well.

00:11:40.165 --> 00:11:41.775
As we've said, it was ...

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:46.860
There were a few months that were a bit harder where I couldn't move properly and ...

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.640
I couldn't speak.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:54.600
I played the next season again and everything ...

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.040
Everything went well.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.320
Everything went well.

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:03.460
You two live very different lives here in New York.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.880
You have a family life.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.880
You don't have a family?

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.280
I have a family. I have a mother and father.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.540
But you're a bachelor in New York, or?

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:18.780
Yeah. I don't have a family life like his, with kids.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.300
So he's actually a quite boring pal?

00:12:21.305 --> 00:12:24.175
Well, I think I would say that ...

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:28.020
Hockey players are pretty boring in general during season.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:30.275
You play four matches a week.

00:12:30.275 --> 00:12:33.335
And you don't have the energy to do a lot of other stuff anyways.

00:12:33.335 --> 00:12:36.475
So you end up in the couch a lot, relaxing.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.680
Recovering after the matches.

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:42.160
We're not living a jetset life.

00:12:42.545 --> 00:12:45.575
How much time do you get on the couch, recovering and relaxing?

00:12:45.575 --> 00:12:47.585
Well, I can remember that time from before I had kids.

00:12:47.585 --> 00:12:48.975
But now it's crazy.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.100
But we spend a lot of time together when we travel.

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:55.440
We have 41 home matches, but we also have 41 matches away from home.

00:12:55.445 --> 00:12:58.635
So the team ends up being together. And then there's also a lot of players who have ...

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:02.620
... their own kids. So when you're at home, you try to ...

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:03.800
... spend time with them.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:09.800
But the last year and a half, it's been more difficult for my oldest daughter to accept that I spend so much time away.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:13.900
And she'll start crying when I leave, and I'll try to explain ...

00:13:14.105 --> 00:13:16.365
... that it's my job and something that I want to do.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:20.300
But I'll leave, and then she'll forget. But the next time she'll cry again.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:24.720
I didn't realize how much we're away before I had children.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.820
Life continued and ...

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:31.655
I did a lot of stuff.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.640
But now you realize how much you're away, with the kids ...

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.100
You lose a lot of time.

00:13:37.435 --> 00:13:40.575
I thought we could finish up here with ...

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:43.260
I know that you're both very competitive.

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:46.060
So ...

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:49.460
I thought it might be cool to se you in action.

00:13:49.625 --> 00:13:52.405
But that would be a little difficult to arrange here.

00:13:52.405 --> 00:13:54.920
But if it's okay with you guys, I've just got ...

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.440
One of those hockey games.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.860
Can we get that in here?

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:03.120
And this ...

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:07.860
Now. Come here, come here. The thing is ...

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.220
We have got ...

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.215
Unfortunately.

00:14:14.215 --> 00:14:15.635
We've got Rangers players.

00:14:16.245 --> 00:14:19.095
And we've got Sweden.

00:14:19.095 --> 00:14:20.095
Okay.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.960
And we tried really hard to get Norway.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.500
But it was really hard. No one had one ...

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:28.600
With Norway.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:31.680
So this is the closest we'll get. You have to be Rangers, and you have to be Sweden.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.680
That's great!

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:33.320
So ...

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.980
The goalie usually sits on the side!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.440
But what are you doing? Come on!

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:43.620
Are you playing the round?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:47.980
Sick, huh?

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.160
Oh my God!

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.680
Okay. Okay.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:56.980
One.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.520
He just steered it in there.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:14:59.940
Here we go.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:10.340
He's just trying to stall the time now!

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.080
I don't think you're that good?

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.460
But this isn't what we play!

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:19.995
And it's just like in soccer, you have to kill the time.

00:15:19.995 --> 00:15:20.995
No!

00:15:23.545 --> 00:15:24.545
Lovely.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.080
Shouldn't we say that ...

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:29.860
These are two of the best hockey players in the world!

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.120
No!

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.400
Time's up!

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:44.540
Yeah!

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:52.680
Thank you so much!

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:55.640
Henke and Zucca are going to Oslo and Ullevaal stadion next summer.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.640
And you can watch NHL matches in Stockholm in November.

